    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_SliceSqlitePublish",
      "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
      "conformsTo": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0"
      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/slice-sqlite-publish.svg",
      "description": "Build one named slice of a knowledge graph as a SQLite file a browser mounts without parsing, and publish it beside its manifest and its payloads. The contract is `kg-export` §\"Per-slice SQLite\"; the builder is the `slice-sqlite` Tool (`cat-harness/scripts/gen-slice-sqlite.ts`), one table-driven builder with one definition per slice; the search is one page, `slices/search.html?slice=<name>`. Bean `q8ar`.\n\nTHE SIZE IS MEASURED BEFORE THE SLICE IS WIRED, AND THAT IS WHY THIS IS A DIAGRAM. A slice that is wired first and measured afterwards ships whatever it weighs, because by then a manifest, a gate, two deploy steps and a page depend on it. The budget gateway sits between measuring and wiring so that an oversized slice stops with its measurement reported, rather than arriving on a reader's connection.\n\nNO BINARY IS COMMITTED. The file is built at deploy from the tree being published, so the gate cannot compare against a committed copy; it proves determinism (two builds, one sha256) and a row-content digest read back from the file against one computed from the source.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 12,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Build and publish a per-slice SQLite file",
      "nodeCount": 13,
      "sourcePath": "processes/kg/slice-sqlite-publish.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/kg/slice-sqlite-publish.bpmn",
      "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_SliceSqlitePublish/node/Start_Need",
      "summary": "Build one named slice of a knowledge graph as a SQLite file a browser mounts without parsing, and publish it beside its manifest and its payloads."
    },
